      "observed": "The SSD1306 interface-select pins are strapped with BS0 (pin 10) to VCC, BS1 (pin 11) to GND, and BS2 (pin 12) to GND, selecting a mode other than the intended I2C mode.",
      "expected": "The specification says BS0 (pin 10) should be tied to GND, BS1 (pin 11) to VCC, and BS2 (pin 12) to GND, selecting I2C mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "U3 BS0 pin 10, BS1 pin 11, BS2 pin 12; the strap wires connect BS0 to VCC and BS1/BS2 to GND. Sheet /DISPLAY/, page 3.",
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "BS0 (pin 10) → GND; BS1 (pin 11) → VCC; BS2 (pin 12) → GND."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The display is configured for a non-I2C interface, so the MCU's two-wire display signals are unlikely to communicate with it as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U1"],
      "pins": ["U1.19"],
      "nets": ["VBAT"],
      "observed": "The STM32L476 VBAT pin (pin 19) is marked no-connect.",
      "expected": "With no separate backup battery shown, VBAT should be connected to VCC so the MCU backup domain is powered.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "U1 pin 19, VBAT, has a no-connect marker. Sheet /, page 1."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU backup domain, including RTC/backup registers when used, will not be powered; the main MCU may still operate.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The OLED interface-select straps do not match the specified I2C configuration, which is likely to prevent the display from working as intended. The MCU's VBAT pin is also explicitly left unconnected despite no backup battery being shown."
}

